// The orthographic silhouette of a sphere is always a circle of radius R centered at (0,0)
// in this same projection space -- a viewer-independent fact of parallel projection, not
// tuned by eye. This is the true limb/horizon line, in the SAME coordinate space and units
// as heroEarthPath above, so it can share the exact viewBox + preserveAspectRatio transform
// and stay physically consistent with the coastline at every breakpoint. Sampled at a uniform
// ANGULAR step (not a uniform y-step): near the pole the circle's tangent is nearly vertical,
// so equal steps in y cover wildly unequal amounts of arc there (one y-step covered 8+ degrees
